When eating a Hershey's Kiss, there should be
some chance of getting the foil wrapper off
intact, if your Dex is good, in which case you
have a one-use (good for only one zap that makes
it past your AC) amulet of reflection.

When eating chocolate, there should be some chance
of "breaking out in hives". If your luck is bad,
this could be multiple swarms of killer bees
generated under the usual random monster rules
(usually out of sight on the level). If your luck is
good, a beehive could coalesce around you, full of
sleeping bees, including a queen bee, and lumps of
royal jelly, just as if the room had originally been
a beehive.

When eating candy bars, there should be some tiny
chance you found a Wonka Bar with a golden
ticket: this, enchanted, might turn into, say,
gloves (or a helm) of reflection (something to ease
the "which reflection do I wear" dilemma with an
extra choice), or perhaps could be a reverse
genocide scroll for gold golems (useful as heck at
a temple altar, gold that carries itself to you).

Thrown, a Hershey's kiss should have a chance to
Tame any female humanoid monster (works for me).

